From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] home toolbar: centre the toolbar items instead of stretching them

Home's GTK4 toolbar is a plain Gtk.Box, and a Gtk.Box gives its children
valign=FILL. Both the search entry and the view buttons therefore grew to
the toolbar's full height instead of sitting at their natural size, which
is what GTK3's Gtk.Toolbar did for its tool items.

Measured on the live guest at 1920x1080, inside the 75px bar:

  search entry     75px -> 42px   (GTK3: 38px)
  selection box    73px -> 65px   (GTK3: 52px)

The stretched entry is the "too tall" search field. The stretched view
buttons are the clipped selection chrome: a checked Sugar tool button
paints its background over its whole allocation, so the selected view's
frame ran the full height of the bar and was cut off by the bar edges
rather than framing the icon.

--- a/src/jarabe/desktop/viewtoolbar.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/desktop/viewtoolbar.py
@@ -75,7 +75,13 @@
         self.search_entry.set_width_chars(25)
         self.search_entry.connect('activate', self._entry_activated_cb)
         self.search_entry.connect('changed', self._entry_changed_cb)
-        
+
+        # This toolbar is a plain Gtk.Box, whose children default to
+        # valign=FILL, so the entry grew to the toolbar's whole 75px
+        # height. GTK3's Gtk.Toolbar centred its items at their natural
+        # size; match that.
+        self.search_entry.set_valign(Gtk.Align.CENTER)
+
         self.append(self.search_entry)
         self.search_entry.set_visible(True)
 
@@ -101,6 +107,11 @@
         toolitem = Gtk.Box()
         toolitem.append(self._button_box)
         toolitem.set_visible(True)
+        # Same reason as the entry: stretched view buttons painted their
+        # selected background over the full toolbar height, so the
+        # selection ran behind the bar edges instead of framing the icon.
+        self._button_box.set_valign(Gtk.Align.CENTER)
+        toolitem.set_valign(Gtk.Align.CENTER)
         self.append(toolitem)
 
         self._add_separator()
